      "writtenOn": "2025-08-28T13:27:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right. In C TF-A the SCR_EL3.FIQ is not necessarily set when the normal world is running if there is no secure payload. In RF-A we have a fixed routing model, so these line can be indeed removed.\nHaving the SCR_EL3.FIQ set is otherwise crucial, otherwise the WFI would hang up forever if the interrupt is not router into the same EL.\nSee original patch here: https://review.trustedfirmware.org/c/TF-A/trusted-firmware-a/+/11253",
